# Copy to `.env.local` (which git ignores) to point the tests somewhere other than their defaults.
# `npm test` reads `.env.local` when it exists. NOTHING here is needed: run `npm run corpus:sync` once and
# the real-content tests read the current official AuroraLegacy/elements from `.corpus/`, with no
# environment at all. A test whose data is not there is skipped and says how to get it.
#
# Once a variable is set, a path that does not exist fails the run instead of skipping it, because a
# skipped test is a green one. Never commit a real value: a path names a person's machine and
# version-control history is permanent.

# Read a different AuroraLegacy.index than `.corpus/AuroraLegacy.index`. If it is an Aurora install
# (under its `custom/` folder) leave the layout at its default; if it is a git checkout, say so and give
# its root.
# INCUDO_AURORA_INDEX="/path/to/AuroraLegacy.index"
# INCUDO_CORPUS_LAYOUT=repository
# INCUDO_CORPUS_ROOT="/path/to/checkout"

# A folder of `.dnd5e` saves instead of `tools/verify/fixtures/saves/`. Transitional: it is removed once
# the generic sample saves of docs/SAMPLE-SAVES.md are in the repository. Your own saves are personal
# data and can never be committed, so tests that read them only run where you put them.
# INCUDO_AURORA_SAVES="/path/to/your/saves"

# Print every difference the Aurora oracle finds, for chasing an `element-extra`.
# INCUDO_ORACLE_DETAIL=1

# Tell an engine change from an upstream change, on the same `.corpus/` commit: write a snapshot with the
# base engine, then fail on any difference from it with yours.
# INCUDO_ORACLE_SNAPSHOT=/tmp/oracle-base.json
# INCUDO_ORACLE_BASELINE=/tmp/oracle-base.json
